{
  "id": 440679385,
  "iid": 22801,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "btl2cap: Add BR/EDR SM to the list of fixed channels",
  "description": "**EDIT**: \"Display as Packet Details\" was introduced in Wireshark 4.6.0 and so made much of the original merge request unnecessary. This now merely adds the BR/EDR SM channel to the list of fixed channels and corrects the CID column display for `L2CAP_FLOW_CONTROL_CREDIT_IND`.\n\nA sample capture has also been attached: [bearer_error_mini.snoop](/uploads/f94b76d647c711143acbaac82ce74903/bearer_error_mini.snoop)\n\n---\n\n\nCurrently, applying the L2CAP CID as a column shows the following in the Packet List pane: \n\n![image](/uploads/7d93861c616a5e9021cb9ee4c080d0b6/image.png){width=900 height=176}\n\nFor dynamically allocated CIDs, all one sees is a generic \"Dynamically Allocated Channel\" -- the value isn't shown, which is very inconvenient for analysis, especially when tracking transactions across multiple channels / bearers.\n\nIt would be much nicer to see the CID value alongside any interpretation of it. So it looks like so now:\n\n![image](/uploads/8b8a2640fe836d3489dfd65c8ed81486/image.png){width=900 height=176}\n\nThis also required the correction of the L2CAP_FLOW_CONTROL_CREDIT_IND parsing to use the Source CID field (`hf_btl2cap_scid`) as described in the core spec -- instead of the CID field (`hf_btl2cap_cid`) which is reserved for the CID from the PDU's L2CAP header.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2025-12-15T21:18:57.110Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-12-17T10:49:30.647Z",
